<article class="wrap">

  <p>Without exception, the most pervasive technical complaint encountered across post-production training forums sounds identical to this: "My color grading looked rich and balanced inside DaVinci Resolve, but upon uploading to YouTube, the shadows washed out and skin tones turned pale." Or alternatively: "Why do my Instagram Reels appear soft and micro-blocked even though I exported directly in 4K resolution?" Both operational failures originate from an identical architectural discrepancy: <strong>your DaVinci Resolve Delivery page configurations are actively clashing with automated social platform compression engines.</strong> Let us break down exact, professional export specifications tailored specifically for YouTube, Instagram Reels, and TikTok—and examine the mechanical reasons why improper encoding degrades visual cinema.</p>

