        <tr><th>Observed Technical Anomaly</th><th>Verified Engineering Fix</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Colors render pale or washed-out post-upload</td><td>Toggle Delivery page gamma tags between Rec.709-A and Gamma 2.4, re-export, and review on target demographic display devices.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Vertical Reel uploads appear mushy or blurred</td><td>Restrict output resolutions to native 1080×1920, lower bitrates until file size drops beneath 50MB, and enforce CBR rate controls.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Audio falls gradually out of sync over time</td><td>Transition export parameters from VBR to CBR—variable rate fluctuations occasionally trigger micro-sync drift during aggressive platform transcoding.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rendering aborts or crashes mid-timeline</td><td>Temporarily disable hardware encoding (switch dropdown to "Native"), close extraneous background applications, and re-try. If crashes persist, split rendering tasks across distinct marked point segments.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Exported output file size is unmanageably large</td><td>Lower manual bitrate parameters, transition from H.264 to advanced H.265 compression (for YouTube delivery), or export multi-part archival episodes.</td></tr>
